  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ConformanceLevel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">mz:ConformanceLevel</rdfs:label>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Specializes"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0028-conformance-levels FR-001</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>A level is a concept of a code list. ISO/IEC 33020 (process capability levels, to verify) and CMMI's maturity levels (to verify) were examined: they define levels of process capability and publish no IRI for them.</mz:justification>
    <mz:mappingRelation>subClassOf</mz:mappingRelation>
    <mz:standardTerm>http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept</mz:standardTerm>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#ConformanceLevel</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ConformanceRequirement">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">mz:ConformanceRequirement</rdfs:label>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Specializes"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0028-conformance-levels FR-002</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>A requirement of a level is a concept of a code list; the standards the requirements point at (RFC 2119, EARS, Gherkin, OSCAL) are named in their definitions and in their specifications.</mz:justification>
    <mz:mappingRelation>subClassOf</mz:mappingRelation>
    <mz:standardTerm>http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept</mz:standardTerm>
